      "side": 1,
      "message": "In this CL, we introduced a conservative method to disable `allow_ref_frame_mvs` based on tpl and motion field data for low-complexity decode . The threshold is increased for speed 3 to improve decoder speed-up. This speed feature is enabled specifically for HDRES.\n\nPerformance results of encoder and decoder for the streams generated\nwith low complexity decode enabled are as follows:\n```\n                       Instruction Count                                                                 \n                          Reduction(%)                   BD-Rate Loss(%)                       Time Reduction(%)\ncpu-used  Resolution    Encoder   Decoder    avg.psnr   ovr.psnr    ssim     vmaf   vmaf_neg    dav1d Decoder   \n   1        HDRES2       4.590     10.943      0.7741     0.7971   0.7365   0.8788   0.8520      10.573\n   2        HDRES2       4.644      9.276      0.7775     0.8051   0.7687   0.8906   0.8894       9.197\n   3        HDRES2       2.894      8.336      0.7344     0.8309   0.7919   0.8053   0.7793       7.991\n```\nThe instruction count reduction specified has been measured using command:\n`$ perf stat -e instructions:u ./aomenc …`\n`$ perf stat -e instructions:u ./dav1d --cpumask avx2 …`\nThe decode time is measured using command\n`time taskset -c 0  ./dav1d  --cpumask avx2 …`\n\nWe have verified that this CL produces no noticeable artifacts for the max-drop contents.",
      "revId": "52e8fbfdb9957c62497259bf9a534c07d85bc5dd",
      "serverId": "e5514cf8-2d6e-3e29-adb4-24cd6dde4bf0"
    },
